{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gmfqwcr6tey546a4kn3c6sgkhlcqyoii3sccig7kgm4e5ltmfuhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` is one translation unit exporting a single symbol, `tritanopia`, taking a by-value 3-byte `{u8,u8,u8}` struct. Five `static` helpers form the pipeline: normalise → remove sRGB gamma → 3×3 tritanopia matrix → re-apply gamma → denormalise.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C exports exactly 1 symbol (`tritanopia`); Rust exports it. Symbol diff **empty**; 0 missing non-libc undefined symbols. Nothing needed translating — no module was skipped, and no stubs were added.\n- **Phase B** — all 39 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass (28 branch signatures + 11 shape rows), 42,705 randomized differential checks. Decisively: **all 16,777,216 inputs byte-identical**. Since the entire public input domain is 3 bytes, this isn't a sample — it's a complete proof of equivalence.\n- **Phase C** — all 11 `ERRORS.md` rows have passing tests.\n- **All configurations** — dev/release × default/`--no-default-features` (no `[features]` table exists). 96 test executions, all green, via `verify.sh`.\n\n## Things worth flagging\n\n**Two bugs were in my own harness, not the translation** — both would have produced false passes:\n\n1. `cargo test --test phase_b` does **not** rebuild a `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` library, because integration tests reach it only through `dlopen`. My first mutation run \"passed\" against a **stale `.so` from 20 minutes earlier**. I added an mtime staleness guard that hard-fails, and verified it fires.\n2. The symbol-parity check wrote `nm` output to `/tmp`, which is read-only in this sandbox — `comm` compared two empty files and printed `OK: all  C symbol(s)`. Now uses a writable scratch dir and fails if `nm` reports zero symbols.\n\n**The translation was already correct.** I made no changes to `src/lib.rs`. Rather than just reporting green, I mutation-tested the suite (14 plausible mistranslations): **9 caught, 5 provably equivalent, 0 unexplained survivors**. The caught set includes the one that actually matters here — the C's `(unsigned char)` cast of an out-of-range float compiles to `cvttss2si %eax` + `mov %al`, which **wraps**, and this is reachable from ordinary input (the `cbDenorm` argument ranges over `[-419.23, 269.28]`, affecting 1.8M of 50.3M output channels). A translation using Rust's saturating `as u8` or a `clamp` would be wrong for those — the existing `f32_to_u8_c_cast` handles it correctly.\n\nTwo of the \"surviving\" mutants are worth knowing about as facts about the C:\n- The red row's two coefficients `0.12739886310880f` and `0.12739886341072f` **round to the identical f32** (`0x3e0274d9`) — they are the same number, so swapping them is a no-op.\n- `>` vs `>=` at the `0.04045` threshold is unobservable: `0.04045 × 255 = 10.31475` isn't an integer, so equality is unreachable.\n\nThe Rust keeps the verbatim literals regardless, staying faithful to the source even where fidelity can't be observed.\n\nArtifacts added: `translation/{SYMBOLS,ERRORS,CONFIGS}.md`, `translation/tests/{common/mod.rs,phase_b.rs,phase_c.rs}`, `translation/tests/data/` (witness data + its generators), `verify.sh`, `mutants.py`, `equivalence_proofs.py`. `c_src/` is unmodified (checksums confirmed; only `c_src/build/` was created)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":837,"cache_read_input_tokens":119756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":837,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c6b5ddc-198f-4d5c-ae07-c94e211c2ebc","uuid":"aee368d6-a693-438b-a9c7-3b9113eef674","timestamp":"2026-08-27T02:35:03.058Z"}
